{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-descartes-braid-structure-generality","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:descartes-braid-structure-generality","kind":"remark","title":"Base-ring generality and the $\\mathfrak{p}$-adic realisation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-descartes-braid-structure","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-p-adic-realisation"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-descartes-braid-structure","tags":["archimedean-universe","braid-group","dic3"],"text":"descartes-braid-structure-generality.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"rem:descartes-braid-structure-generality\"></a>\n<strong>Remark.</strong> <em>Base-ring generality and the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}</code>-adic realisation</em></p>\n<p>The braid-group structure of <a href=\"#cor:descartes-braid-structure\">a Descartes universe</a> holds over any base ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">30 \\in R^{\\times}</code>. It applies directly to the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}</code>-adic realisation (<a href=\"#ex:p-adic-realisation\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>-adic realisation</a>), where knot complements and skein relations remain unavailable.</p>\n"}
